1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,850
So today we're looking at why thumbnails fail at feed size.

2
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:07,550
Thumbnails need contrast, a face, and three words at most.

3
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:08,850
um

4
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:11,150
Most thumbnails use too many words.

5
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:14,400
Most thumbnails use too many words, and they blur.

6
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:18,100
Big faces read at small sizes, tiny text does not.

7
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:25,600
Now let's talk titles and how they truncate on mobile.

8
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:29,050
Titles cut at forty characters on a phone feed.

9
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:32,850
Put the subject first so the cut never loses it.

10
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:40,150
Finally, retention: the first fifteen seconds decide everything.

11
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:43,500
Open a question the viewer cannot close without watching.

12
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,950
Then deliver the payoff you promised in the hook.
